<title>MALAYSIA: MIDF up 2.64 pct after not selling bank.</title>
<headline>MIDF up 2.64 pct after not selling bank.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Malaysian Industrial Development Finance Bhd (MIDF) rose 2.64 percent in early trading following its Friday announcement of not selling its banking unit.</p>
<p>Around 15 minutes into the opening, the stock was up 12 cents to 4.66 ringgit.  </p>
<p>Financial group MIDF said it does not intend to sell its 78.4 percent stake in the 41-branch Oriental Bank Bhd.</p>
<p>Malaysia's largest conglomerate Sime Darby Bhd had announced in December it had approval from the central bank to start negotiating with MIDF to buy a 51 percent stake in Oriental.</p>
<p>Sime stock was up 10 cents to 9.35 ringgit.</p>
</text>
